# Who has to approve what, when "Require review from Code Owners" is on in the
# branch protection rule for `main`. See the Branch protection section of the
# README for the settings this file is useless without.
#
# The point of this file is not ownership -- there is one maintainer. It is that
# an agent can open a pull request touching anything, and there are three kinds
# of file where a human must be in the loop no matter how good the automated
# review looked:
#
#   1. the automation itself, because a PR that edits the reviewer can pass it
#   2. the tests, because weakening one is how a red build turns green
#   3. money, keys and identity control, where a wrong merge is not revertible
#
# Replace @devdudeio with a team (e.g. @chainvue/maintainers) when there is one;
# the paths stay as they are.

# Everything, by default.
*                           @devdudeio

# --- 1. the automation reviewing the automation ------------------------------
/.github/                   @devdudeio
/.github/workflows/         @devdudeio
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @devdudeio
/.github/claude-risk-paths.yml @devdudeio
/scripts/                   @devdudeio
/CLAUDE.md                  @devdudeio

# --- 2. the tests ------------------------------------------------------------
# An agent may add tests here freely; it may not quietly change what the
# existing ones assert. Snapshots are listed separately because accepting a
# snapshot is a one-command way to make a rendering regression look intentional.
/tests/                     @devdudeio
/tests/snapshots/           @devdudeio
/fixtures/                  @devdudeio

# --- 3. money, keys, identity ------------------------------------------------
/src/keystore.rs            @devdudeio
/src/cmd/key.rs             @devdudeio
/src/cmd/send.rs            @devdudeio
/src/cmd/airgap.rs          @devdudeio
/src/cmd/id.rs              @devdudeio
/src/cmd/lifecycle.rs       @devdudeio
/src/payload.rs             @devdudeio
/src/config.rs              @devdudeio
/src/node.rs                @devdudeio

# --- supply chain ------------------------------------------------------------
# The SDK is pinned by rev. Moving that pin changes every signature this program
# produces, and no test in this repo can tell you it was safe.
/Cargo.toml                 @devdudeio
/Cargo.lock                 @devdudeio
/rust-toolchain.toml        @devdudeio
/Makefile                   @devdudeio
